"""Leading with AI (Leadership Edition), Session 5: Generative AI: how chatbots write, and why they sometimes invent.  Written 12 November 2026.

Pattern (pilot Session 2): recall and a hook with a real case; the idea as a ladder of pictures with no maths; the six-industry tour and
two good-use case stories, then the failures (invented citations, liability); recorded demonstrations; your people; questions to ask;
the portfolio hands-on; the decision; the take-away.

Cases (research/*.md): LGL-01 Mata v Avianca (hook and timeline), LGL-02 and PUB-09 Mavundla, LGL-04 Deloitte Australia (timeline),
RTL-01 Air Canada and RTL-02 DPD (liability), EDU-01 and PUB-08 Edo State tutoring (case), AGR-04 Farmer.Chat (case), HLT-01 Penda Health
(tour, told in full in Session 0), BNK-10 Klarna, TEL-10 Vodacom and Google Cloud, MFG-09 Nestle NesGPT (tour).  Swap: MFG-02 (Coca-Cola's
AI video advert) is left out because today is about text; MFG-09 gives the FMCG tile a text assistant instead.
Demonstrations: GPT-2 small recorded runs in demo_runs/s05/ (results.json, 6 November 2026, transformers 5.22.1; logits_run_2026-11-11.json,
11 November 2026, which matches); the made-up court case question from the Executive Edition Case Runs F2a (Claude, two fresh sessions,
4 November 2026; summarised in demo_runs/s10_scoring.md).  Nile Valley Foods is fictional.
"""

