    cover_note='Welcome back. In Session 4 we saw AI that understands language: it sorts messages, finds a clause by meaning, translates and summarises. Today we move from AI that reads to AI that writes, the chatbots many of your staff already use. Our question: why does a chatbot sound so sure, and when can I trust what it writes? We start in a New York court, build the idea from drawings, with no maths, look inside a real model’s choices, tour six industries, and see where chatbots help and where they invent. Then you add a drafting task of your own to your portfolio.',
